## Track your mood

Keep a **daily mood diary or app**. Over time, you may see what triggers highs and lows, such as poor sleep, stress or the seasons.

## Keep a steady routine

Go to bed and get up at the same time, eat regularly and keep some structure to your week. Routine helps keep mood steadier.

## During highs

- pause before **big decisions** or large purchases
- protect your **sleep**, even if you do not feel tired

## During lows

- set **small, achievable goals**
- stay **connected** with people you trust
- be kind to yourself. Lows pass

## Alcohol and drugs

They can make mood swings more intense and harder to predict.

## Support

**Bipolar UK** supports people with cyclothymia as well as bipolar disorder, through peer groups and an online community.
